== HF
# HF: the shape of each write site of `cur_prefix` (H3's 25), by (file, fn, site = the site's ordinal in the fn in
# source order). A site is a `mem::replace` / `take` / `swap` opener, a clone save (`let b = <recv>.cur_prefix.clone()`
# that some `cur_prefix = b` restores), a struct-literal init, or `stray` (a write no region holds). Computed: FORM,
# BIND (the saved binding), ARG (the opener's text argument, as tokens), BLOCK (the opener's block: a path from the fn
# body, `s<i>` a statement from the block's first, a construct then / else / arm<j> / for / while / loop / blk /
# closure / letelse), OPENER (`s<i>` in BLOCK), RESTORES (each `cur_prefix = BIND` in the region = BLOCK after the
# opener ; its first step `e<k>` counted back from BLOCK's last statement, e0 = the last), REPOINTS (`<rhs>@<pos>`,
# any other assignment there), SAME (every restore a statement of BLOCK itself), EXITS (the `return` / `?` / `break` /
# `continue` between the opener and the last restore: `@<pos>` when it leaves the region, `(local)` / `(closure)`
# counted when its target is inside), PATHS (every path from the opener to the region's end or out of it, by where it
# leaves, with its state: r<n> = n restores, `!` = cur re-pointed and not restored), NEST (calls between the opener
# and the last restore of a fn that writes cur, `dyn:<name>` a call of a parameter or local). HAND: PLAN8 (plan8
# H3's class: FIT / NOT-FIT / CTOR) and READ (what the syntax leaves to a reader: a dyn call's body, a clone save, an
# exit out of the region, a path that is not r1 ; the test requires it there). Not seen: a panic (only the four
# diverging macros end a path), a write through a `&mut String` bound earlier, a macro that does not parse.
# LS2a: FORM is the funnel entry's name (H3's note), `scope_restore(b)` / `scope_repoint(x)` read as `cur_prefix = b / x`.
file	fn	site	form	bind	arg	block	opener	restores	repoints	same	exits	paths	nest	PLAN8	READ
cont_array.rs	check_whole_array_sole_writer	1	scope_swap_empty	saved	-	body	s11	e0	prefix@e1/for/s0	yes	-	end=r1	-	NOT-FIT	-
cont_var.rs	check_var_cont_assign_sole_writer	1	scope_swap_empty	saved	-	body	s10	e0	a.prefix.clone()@e3/for/s2,a.prefix.clone()@e1/for/s1/then/s1	yes	continue(local)x1	end=r1	-	NOT-FIT	-
cover_synth.rs	materialize_cover	1	scope_swap_text	saved_prefix	cov.scope.clone()	s1/for	s0	e0	-	yes	-	end=r1	-	FIT	-
dead_arm.rs	settle_dead_arm	1	scope_swap_text	prefix	d.prefix	s4/for	s2	e0	-	yes	-	end=r1	-	FIT	-
driver.rs	new	1	init	-	lexscope::Scopes::new()	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	CTOR	-
